{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/832439-need-advice-on-new-homebrewed-gift","id":832439,"title":"Need advice on new homebrewed gift.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-18T04:23:41-08:00","id":832439,"title":"Need advice on new homebrewed gift.","content":"I need your help with figuring out what level is appropriate for a gift that mimics the Armor Charm (2nd edition) as in that it allows the Garou to auto-soak damage.<br /> <br /> My idea would be something either<br /> &quot;The Garou spends a point of Gnosis and rolls Stamina+Survival, each success allows the Garou to automatically soak one level of damage for the remainder of the scene.&quot;<br /> or &quot;For each point of Gnosis spent the Garou may automatically soak one level of damage for the remainder of the scene.&quot;<br /> or perhaps a combination of the two, as in &quot;The Garou spends one or more points of Gnosis and rolls Stamina+Survival, for each Gnosis spent the Garou may automatically soak on level of damage up to the number of successes on the roll for the remainder of the scene.&quot;<br /> <br /> One could also mimic the Revised Ed. Armor Charm and say that &quot;By spending two points of Gnosis, the Garous gains an additional soak pool equal to its Gnosis for the remained of the scene&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> What do you guys think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T06:54:28-08:00","id":832488,"title":"","content":"Luna's Armour, Troll Skin and Steel Fur are the benchmark gifts for all soak gifts. Better then these, most gifts should not be, unless significantly higher in level.<br /> <br /> All three gifts cost one point (Gnosis or Willpower) to grant successes to the soak dice pool.<br /> <br /> As for automatic soak, there is Sigurd's Stide. It is not really a good benchmark, since it has a low difficult and the soak is only against fire damage (albeit there it is automatic).<br /> Some higher level gifts might also be able to ignore certain damage, as is a level 5 fetish.<br /> <br /> <br /> I would go for a high cost (one per automatic success) and limit there number (up to the successes on activation roll). I would also use a high difficulty. And obviously one can only have as many automatic successes as one has soak dice, so if you have zero dice to soak silver, you still can't soak it.<br /> But if you have 10 against agg damage, and four automatic successes you still roll six dice to soak any damage exceeding 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T09:30:47-08:00","id":832555,"title":"","content":"I don't think this is a very wise gift to give, it treads on ground already well taken. <br /> <br /> <br /> That said, I'd love to see an armour gift that uses rage. <br /> Spend a rage to make a magnetic pulse that repels all metal/energy attacks for a turn. <br /> Or a torrent of air that wards things away from you. Air or magnetic spirit. What'ya think? <br /> not sure if extra soak dice or an increase in difficulty to hit/decrease in difficulty to soak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T14:25:07-08:00","id":832756,"title":"","content":"Get of Fenris have a lvl 4 gift that repels and shatters any weapon made of metal that strikes them. It's in the DA: W book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}